Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:04.504
Russia says that it thwarted a Ukrainian
attack on one of its reconnaissance ships.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.440
But there's new video.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.108
Is that true?

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.242
What they said

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.580
Well,
it seems as though it potentially isn't.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.282
The Ukrainian certainly have
a very different point of view of that.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.752
Now, it seems they have the video,
but it seems to back that up.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.419
And you're absolutely right.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.889
At first the Russians had said
that there was an attack with sea drones.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.391
Those are essentially unmanned surface

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:27.761
vessels on one of their main intelligence
ships in the Black Sea.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:31.831
And the Russians showed a video of
their ship destroying one of those drones.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:35.835
But the Ukrainians came with a video today
which seems to show another drone moving

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:39.739
towards that ship and coming towards
that ship, potentially hitting it.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:43.009
We're not sure what exactly the damage is,
but in that video,

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:46.613
which is quite dramatic,
you can see someone from the Russian ship

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:50.116
firing at that sea drone,
seemingly trying to stop it.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.319
And this potentially could be a big blow
to the Russians because, of course,

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.156
it shows on the one hand
that their ships really aren't safe

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:59.726
from the Ukrainians in the Black Sea,
but also the ship that was hit.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.761
It's called the Ivan Horse.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:05.532
And it's actually one of the most modern
intelligence ships that the Russians have.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.334
It only went into service in 20, 20, 18.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:12.138
So that potentially in itself
could be a big blow and another big

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.775
blow to the Russian
navy in the war against Ukraine Jake.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.911
All right, Fred Pleitgen in Kiev, Ukraine,
thanks so much.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.713
A series of drone and missile strikes
reported across Ukraine,

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.083
including the capital region of key
president.

